---
// Standalone page rather than the BlogPost layout. That layout stamps a pubDate
// and a hero image on whatever it wraps, which is why this page used to claim it
// was published in August 2021. An About page is not a dated post.
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="About — Narayan Lekhi"
			description="A high school student working in sports analytics, bringing basic analytics to his school's basketball team."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="band heading-band">
				<div class="band-inner band-inner--wide at-edge">
					<h1>About</h1>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="band tight">
				<div class="band-inner at-edge">
					<p>
						I'm a high school student working in sports analytics. My projects start with
						something I notice during games and can't find answers to.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- The thesis of the page gets the green band. Body size, so it reads as
			     emphasis rather than a second headline. -->
			<div class="band band--green">
				<div class="band-inner at-step">
					<p>
						Right now I'm bringing basic analytics to my school's basketball team. Half of
						the work is the data analysis and the other more important half is
						translation. A coach in a timeout or a player making a decision at a
						crossroads has no use for a regression table. So it's my job to present these
						findings in a digestible format where it becomes beneficial.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="band">
				<div class="band-inner at-deep">
					<p>
						I also lead the sports analytics club at my school where I spearhead
						discussions and teach other students who are interested in sports beyond the
						box score. It's a place where not only do I teach, but I gain new perspective
						through the lens of other students. After all, there's a lot I haven't learned
						yet, which is why I want to grow and share as much of my journey as I can.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
<style>
	.heading-band {
		padding-block: var(--space-2xl) var(--space-m);
	}
	h1 {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}
	.tight {
		padding-block: var(--space-m) var(--space-xl);
	}
	p {
		margin: 0;
	}
</style>
